By \Cref{lemma:low_frequency_G}, the following convergence holds:  egin{displaymath} \lim \limits_{\eta 	o +\infty} \sup_{s \in [0, t]} \sup_{|\xi| \le \Xi} \| G(s, \xi, \eta) \| = 0. \end{displaymath} Due to the stiff well-posedness of \cref{eq}, there exists a constant $K_1 > 0$ such that  egin{displaymath} \|{\hat{u}(s, \xi, \eta)}\| \le K_1 \|{\hat{U}_0(\xi)}\|, \end{displaymath} for each $s \ge 0$, $\xi \in \mathbb{R}^d$ and $\eta \ge 0$. Therefore,  egin{multline*} 
orm{  ig( \hat{u}(t, \cdot, \eta) - \exp(H_{11} t) \hat{u}_0  ig) \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi} }_{L^2} \ \le 
orm{ G(t, \cdot, \eta) \hat{v}_0 \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi} }_{L^2} + \int_0^t 
orm{ G(t-s, \cdot, \eta) H_{21} \hat{u}(s, \cdot, \eta) \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi} }_{L^2} \,\mathrm{d} s \ \le \sup_{s \in [0, t]} \sup_{|\xi| \le \Xi} \| G(s, \xi, \eta) \| \cdot  igg( \| \hat{v}_0 \|_{L^2} + t K_1 \sup_{|\xi| \le \Xi} \| H_{21}(\xi, 0) \| \cdot \| \hat{U}_0 \|_{L^2}  igg), \end{multline*} which yields the desired convergence. Let us now consider the case when the matrix sets $\mathcal{F}_1$ and $\mathcal{F}_2$ are uniformly quasi-stable. Note that  egin{multline*} 
orm{  ig( \hat{u}(t, \cdot, \eta) - \exp(H_{11} t) \hat{u}_0  ig) \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi(\eta)} }_{L^2} \ \le 
orm{ G(t, \cdot, \eta) \hat{v}_0 \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi(\eta)} }_{L^2} + \int_0^t 
orm{ G(t-s, \cdot, \eta) H_{21} \hat{u}(s, \cdot, \eta) \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi(\eta)} }_{L^2} \,\mathrm{d} s. \end{multline*} By \Cref{lemma:low_frequency_G}, the first right-hand term in this inequality can be bounded by  egin{displaymath} 
orm{ G(t, \cdot, \eta) \hat{v}_0 \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi(\eta)} }_{L^2} \le  rac{	ilde{C} e^t}{\eta} \|v_0\|_{H^1} \log(\eta 	ilde{\delta} + 1), \end{displaymath} and the integrand in the integral term of this inequality can be estimated as follows:  egin{displaymath} 
